WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.980
Hulk has clashed with the Avengers countless
times, but usually, it's out of love.

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:09.660
Earth's Mightiest Heroes are often just trying
to protect innocent people from Hulk's rampages.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.250
Fair enough, but sometimes, the Avengers could
just be super-jerks to the Green Goliath.

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:21.100
While Hulk was technically one of the original
Avengers in 1963's Avengers #1, the group's

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.860
founding was largely a hunt for the man-monster.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:29.160
Much like the movie adaptation, Avengers #1
saw Loki accidentally forming the Avengers

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.920
while trying to use Hulk to defeat his half-brother
Thor.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:36.320
When Loki shows up, the Hulk is in hiding,
acting as a performer in a circus.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.360
Later, when the Hulk uses his colossal strength
to save a train on a broken track, Loki uses

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.140
his illusions to make it appear the Hulk was
the culprit who wrecked the tracks in the

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.000
first place.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.640
Rick Jones and his Teen Brigade call out with
ham radios to any heroes who could help stem

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.340
the Hulk's threat and Iron Man, Ant-Man, and
the Wasp answer.

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:59.019
The three soon-to-be-teammates spend most
of Avengers #1 chasing the Hulk and battling

00:00:59.020 --> 00:00:59.960
him in a factory.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.540
Before anyone gets seriously hurt, Thor arrives
with Loki as his prisoner, having figured

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.600
out Loki's scheme.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.800
While the now-iconic cover of Avengers #1
depicts the five original Avengers battling

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.600
Loki, the only one who truly threw down with
him was Thor.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.920
The Hulk did nothing but fight off his attackers,
who believed the lie that the Hulk was nothing

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.560
more than a rampaging beast.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.060
The Hulk's time in the Avengers was short-lived.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.740
He quit at the end of Avengers #2, and considering
everything, it's tough to blame him.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:33.120
In Avengers #2, the team was infiltrated by
an alien villain named the Space Phantom who

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.220
could mimic the appearance of different heroes.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:40.280
Unsurprisingly, he chose the Hulk as his victim,
and used the giant green monster to beat up

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.060
the Avengers a bit before switching into a
different body.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.240
When the smoke cleared and everyone realized
what had happened, the Hulk was angry at what

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.160
the Avengers said about him when they believed
they were fighting him.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.160
"Earth hate Hulk."

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.260
"Earth love Hulk!

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.600
They love you, you're one of the Avengers,
one of the team!

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.100
Our friend!

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.240
This is what friends do, they support each
other."

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:03.080
That could have been the end of it, but in
Avengers #3, the Avengers actively hunted

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.980
the Hulk and battled him once more.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:09.360
The Hulk fought them off and eventually allied
himself with the aquatic outcast Namor the

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.020
Sub-Mariner in an attempt to destroy the team
and get them off his back.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.080
In 1988, the High Evolutionary was ticking
off the whole Marvel Universe in an event

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:22.620
called Evolutionary War, which ran through
Marvel's annuals.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:28.560
The finale was in Avengers Annual #17, but
there was a problem: the Avengers had disbanded.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.820
An alarm summoned a band of reserve Avengers
anyway.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:36.500
At the end of Incredible Hulk #350, Hulk is
finishing an epic battle with The Thing of

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:41.390
the Fantastic Four, when X-Men's Beast happens
upon the Hulk and strong-arms him into helping

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:42.260
the Avengers.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:46.240
At the time, most of the world believed the
Hulk had died in a gamma bomb explosion a

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.680
few issues earlier… except he didn't.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:53.320
Instead, a gray, more intelligent version
of the Hulk had survived and relocated to

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.240
Las Vegas, and he liked the world thinking
he was dead.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.780
So, the Beast did exactly what any honorable,
heroic member of the Avengers and the X-Men

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:05.390
would do: He told the Hulk if he didn't help
the Avengers, he'd reveal to the entire world

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.280
that he was still alive, making him a wanted
man-monster once more.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.180
How heroic.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.460
It's no secret the Hulk tends to hold a grudge.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:24.080
But in Marvel Comics, the Hulk isn't the only
one who knows how to hold onto a beef.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:29.480
In 1995's Incredible Hulk #434, the Avengers
threw the first punch.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.090
The issue immediately followed the Over the
Edge event, in which Nick Fury has been killed,

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.220
and the Avengers blame the Hulk for Fury's
death.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.780
As soon as the Hulk shows up to the funeral,
the Avengers attack him.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:44.360
It was even the usually rational android Vision
who starts everything by using his phasing

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.860
powers to shove his finger into the Hulk's
brain.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:51.460
Somewhat surprisingly, the Hulk hardly fights
back, uncharacteristically trying to talk

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.640
his way out of a fight.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:59.040
When the Avengers lock horns with the Hulk
in 1986's Incredible Hulk #316, they battle

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.240
a different kind of Hulk.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:05.300
The gamma-powered hero Doc Samson had developed
a method to physically separate Bruce Banner

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.440
from his greener half.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:11.040
As a result, an utterly mindless Hulk was
raging through the New Mexico desert destroying

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.510
everything he saw.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:17.480
That leads the Avengers send their four physically
strongest members - Hercules, Namor, Wonder

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.460
Man, and Iron Man - to stop him.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.320
It makes sense the Avengers would want to
take out such a destructive version of the

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.100
green goliath, but half of the quartet formed
in the desert to tussle with the Hulk don't

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.000
even bother to take it seriously.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.220
Wonder Man acts like the pampered Hollywood
socialite that he was at the time, and Hercules

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.720
in particular treats the whole thing like
a game.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.500
That wouldn't be the last time that the Avengers
attacked the Hulk to prevent untold destruction.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:46.010
During Civil War II, the Inhuman Ulysses'
psychic vision shows the original Hulk on

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:49.180
a rampage, apparently murdering most of Marvel's
heroes.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:53.620
When those heroes confront Banner, they discover
he's researching gamma radiation, and are

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:55.639
less than happy with the implications.

00:04:55.639 --> 00:04:57.880
A huge group of heroes confront Banner.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.390
Because the best thing you can do to someone
with anger issues is surround him with as

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.820
many people as possible while yelling at him.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.740
"Clearly your friend is in desperate need
of help."

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.760
"Yeah, yeah, yeah."

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:12.820
"We realized we also need as many people attacking
this guy as we can possibly get."

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.260
Before anything can be resolved, Hawkeye murders
Bruce Banner.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:16.980
Sort of.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:21.240
A flashback reveals that Banner had actually
created the arrows that Clint Barton used

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:25.040
to kill him, and that he had given them to
the archer in case he should ever need to

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:25.540
be put down.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:30.420
Hawkeye claims he saw Banner's eyes flash
green before he fired off the fatal shot,

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:33.220
but whether or not that was true is left purposefully
ambiguous.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:38.180
While the Avengers and Hulk were both still
stinging from a couple of recent clashes,

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:41.870
Earth's Mightiest and the Hulk were forced
to work together for the Marvel-wide comics

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:42.980
event Onslaught.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:47.240
While things never got violent between Hulk
and his former teammates, it wasn't for lack

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.430
of the Avengers trying.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:53.660
In Incredible Hulk #445, the Hulk gets so
tired of the Avengers giving him dirty looks

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.780
everywhere he went that he tells them so.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:59.780
In spite of Hulk telling them to stop unless
they wanted him to join "the other side,"

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:03.169
the heroes continue to look at him like they
would love nothing more than for the green

00:06:03.169 --> 00:06:04.560
goliath to try something.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:09.020
By the way, treating the Hulk like garbage
during Onslaught wasn't just an Avengers game.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:14.280
After the event finale in Onslaught: Marvel
Universe #1 - when the Hulk provided the decisive

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:19.330
blow against Onslaught by cracking the villain's
supposedly impenetrable armor - the Avengers

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.180
and the Fantastic Four disappear and are presumed
dead.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:26.120
The Hulk is left lying on the ground and the
X-Men just… leave him there.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.400
They don't even mention him.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.180
Without him, Onslaught would have won, but
the heroes didn't seem to care.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:37.080
Not all of the Avengers' unwarranted assaults
on the Hulk occurred in Marvel's heyday.

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:43.389
As recently as 2018, Immortal Hulk #6 ends
with the Avengers tracking down the newly-resurrected

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:44.740
Bruce Banner to capture him.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.140
One of the biggest reasons for their attack
was a battle between the Hulk and the Canadian

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.940
hero Sasquatch in a hospital.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:54.960
Immortal Hulk #7 opens with every indication
that the Avengers are not going to get their

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:55.460
way.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:07:00.460
The Hulk proves more powerful than ever, hitting
Thor so hard that Captain America has to carry

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:01.200
him from the battlefield.

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:06.270
The Hulk rips up yet another Hulkbuster armor
to pieces, and takes out his cousin She-Hulk

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:07.220
with a single punch.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:12.210
Unfortunately for Hulk, Black Panther and
Tony Stark have a powerful energy cannon orbiting

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:15.900
the Earth, ready to take him out if the Avengers
can't do it themselves.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:20.380
Unable to stop him any other way, the Avengers
kill the Hulk with the cannon, knowing that

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:22.420
he'll come back, since he always does.

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:27.920
"Go to sleep go to sleep go to sleep."

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:31.980
Comics aren't the only medium in which the
Avengers treat the Hulk like trash.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:35.960
Sure, usually in the movies when the Hulk
clashes with his teammates, he's the one to

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.740
initiate the throwdown, so it's hard to blame
them.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.020
But what about a scene that isn't a fight?

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.040
What about a scene that was an audience pleaser
in the theaters?

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:48.520
Toward the end of Avengers: Age of Ultron,
after Bruce Banner frees Black Widow from

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:52.560
Ultron's prison, he's ready to go with Widow's
idea to skedaddle and live on the run with

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:53.060
her.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.699
He doesn't seem at all scared of helping the
Avengers fight Ultron, at least not for himself…

00:07:57.699 --> 00:08:01.520
but the last time he transformed it was under
the Scarlet Witch's influence, and he ended

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.300
up going on a deadly rampage.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:05.720
It's something he doesn't want to repeat.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.000
Black Widow takes the choice out of Banner's
hands; she pushes him off a ledge, forcing

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.420
him to transform into the Hulk to save himself.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:13.180
Why?

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.500
"I need the other guy.

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.200
Let's finish the job."

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:26.200
It may have gotten applause in the theater,
but considering how close Bruce and Natasha

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:30.710
had grown, and how harrowing an experience
it is for Banner to transform into the Hulk

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:33.400
and back, Widow's push is a chilling betrayal.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.020
No Asgardian hammer or titanium fist could
wound him more.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.500
And of course who could forget Planet Hulk?

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.300
In 2005, Bruce Banner agrees to help S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.620
take out a dangerous space-based Hydra weapon.

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:58.759
Unfortunately, it's a trap.While the Hydra
threat was presumably real, the primary purpose

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.460
of Hulk's recruitment was to get him into
space.

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:05.240
Once he completes his mission and boards the
shuttle that he thought would take him home,

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.780
the ship heads off in a different direction
and a recorded message plays.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:14.040
Four members of Marvel's Illuminati - Mister
Fantastic, Iron Man, Doctor Strange, and Black

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:18.220
Bolt - appear before the Hulk, explaining
to him that they are sending him away, both

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.220
for his own good and that of the Earth.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.860
The betrayal leads to one of the most memorable
and well-loved Hulk stories of recent memory,

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:25.480
Planet Hulk.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.880
That storyline also leads to the follow-up
revenge story, 2007's World War Hulk, which

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:35.009
sees the Hulk smash all four of his betrayers
as well as a healthy chunk of the rest of

00:09:35.009 --> 00:09:35.940
Marvel's heroes.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:39.800
At the end of the day, there's one thing you
can always count on Hulk to do:

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.960
"Hulk Smash!"

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.440
